The constructor's change has a test of its own, and it does not need
concurrency at all.
An initialising process leaves [[.learnlog/]] in a state no newcomer
can distinguish from a bare directory, and the shortest way to produce
that state on purpose is to make the bare directory.
A [[LearnlogRepo]] built on it must come out with a working
repository---which also means a first run killed halfway through
initialisation is repaired by the next one instead of poisoning the
project.

<<test functions>>=
